# Architecture (Permanent)

## Locked stack (do not fork without explicit product decision)

| Layer | Choice |
| --- | --- |
| API | **NestJS** (Node.js LTS), modular monolith |
| Web | **Next.js** (App Router) + TypeScript |
| Primary DB | **PostgreSQL** — users, businesses, billing, memberships, jobs metadata |
| Cache / Queue | **Redis** — OTP cooldown, cache, BullMQ (or equivalent) queues |
| Document store | **MongoDB** — Document JSON / page trees / version snapshots |
| Auth | Mobile OTP + **JWT** (access; refresh optional) |
| ORM / data | **Prisma** for PostgreSQL; **official `mongodb` driver** for MongoDB (do not introduce TypeORM or Mongoose without ADR) |
| PDF | Server Chromium (Playwright/Puppeteer) or Gotenberg via worker |
| Maps | Leaflet + OSM when Map module enabled |
| Object storage | S3-compatible (MinIO/local disk in dev) for media/fonts |

Monorepo layout (required):

```text
/
  apps/
    api/                 # NestJS
    web/                 # Next.js
  packages/
    document-schema/     # shared Document JSON types/schema (TS)
    shared-types/        # DTOs, entitlement codes, constants
  docs/                  # PRD, ADRs, api, deploy
  .cursor/rules/
```

## Data placement rules

- **PostgreSQL**: transactional tenancy & money — User, Business, Subscription, Plan, Payment, Membership, Audit pointers.
- **Redis**: ephemeral/fast — rate limits, OTP challenge meta, sessions/blacklist if used, queues.
- **MongoDB**: flexible document payloads — `documents`, pages/elements trees, optional render caches keyed by `businessId` + `documentId`.
- Always mirror `businessId` on Mongo documents; never query cross-business without filter.
- Do not invent a fourth primary store without an ADR + rule update.

## Layering (API)

Request → Auth Guard (JWT) → **BusinessContext** → **EntitlementGuard** → Controller → Domain Service → Repositories (PG / Mongo) → Stores.

Rendering: `Document JSON` (Mongo) → HTML/CSS canonical → ExportJob (Redis queue) → PDF/Image.

Never call PDF renderer on the interactive request path for every editor keystroke.

**Non-goal (current version):** DOCX/PPTX Office export — see ADR 025. Do not fork a second layout engine for Word/PowerPoint without product unlock.

## Domain modules (Nest modules)

- `IdentityModule` — User, OTP
- `TenancyModule` — Business, Membership
- `BillingModule` — Plan, Module, Subscription, Payment, Invoice, License
- `ContentModule` — business entities (projects, team, …)
- `AssetsModule` — Media, Fonts
- `DesignModule` — Theme, Template, MasterPage, Blocks
- `DocumentsModule` — Document metadata (PG) + body (Mongo)
- `ExportModule` — ExportJob, Renderer adapters
- `AuditModule` — AuditEvent
- `SystemModule` — health, APP_EDITION config

## Hard boundaries

- No cross-Business queries without `businessId` filter (PG and Mongo).
- No entitlement logic only in Next.js.
- No storing company content inside template rows (templates are structure/style/bindings).
- New sellable features get a **module code** and gate.
- **Dual deployment locked:** `SELF_HOSTED` | `SAAS` via `APP_EDITION` — see `08-dual-deployment.mdc`.
- Stack is **NestJS + Next.js + PostgreSQL + Redis + MongoDB** — do not reintroduce Laravel/PHP/MySQL/Vite-SPA as the primary stack.
